"""Revised ESG classification rules — classifier v1.1.

中文说明：本文件是“修订后的 ESG 词典”的唯一来源。每条规则 = 一个正则表达式 + 类型 + 主题 + 维度 + 理由。
规则按顺序作用于标准化后的 metricOther 文本；一旦匹配，被匹配的片段即被“消耗”，后面更宽泛的规则不能再用它
（例如先把 'product safety' 归为 Extended，再让通用 'safety' 规则运行；先屏蔽 'safety and soundness'）。
`changed` 字段注明该规则在哪个版本新增 / 修改及原因，便于审计（与 Dictionaries/c_change_log.csv 对应）。

kind
  MASK      span neutralised, no evidence (company / segment / product names, homonyms)
  MASKN     span neutralised AND counted as non-ESG evidence (e.g. 'safety and soundness', 'economic environment')
  ESG       Strict ESG evidence (pillar E / S / G, or GEN = multi-pillar ESG/CSR/sustainability)
  EXT       Extended-only stakeholder evidence (customers, product responsibility, community engagement,
            customer-facing service reliability); never Strict
  EXT_AMB   stakeholder meaning possible but unclear -> Strict 0, Extended Unknown
  AMB       ESG meaning possible but unclear -> Strict Unknown (and Extended Unknown); a pillar-specific AMB hit
            also leaves that pillar Unknown when another rule makes the text Strict ESG
  ADJ       ESG-adjacent but excluded by definition (generic compliance/risk/controls/cyber, generic workforce,
            labour negotiations, public affairs, renewable-energy or ESG business lines) -> 0/0 + flag
  NONESG    informative non-ESG content (financial, market, operating, product-development ...)
  NONSPEC   non-specific placeholder (individual / strategic / discretionary ...) -> Unknown
  FILLER    generic words, consumed, no evidence
Decision precedence: ESG > AMB > NONSPEC > (EXT | EXT_AMB | ADJ | NONESG) > nothing matched (Unknown).
"""

R = []
def add(kind, topic, pillar, pattern, conf="high", why="", kw="", changed=""):
    R.append(dict(kind=kind, topic=topic, pillar=pillar, pattern=pattern, confidence=conf, rationale=why, paper_keywords=kw, changed=changed))

